            "new_string": "# use-ai Monorepo\n\nA TypeScript monorepo using Bun for building AI-powered React applications with WebSocket-based AI agent integration.\n\n## Structure\n\n```\n.\n├── packages/\n│   ├── client/          # @use-ai/client - React hooks library for AI integrations\n│   └── server/          # @use-ai/server - WebSocket server for AI agent hosting\n└── apps/\n    └── example/         # Example AI-powered todo list app\n```\n\n## Getting Started\n\n### Install Dependencies\n\n```bash\nbun install\n```\n\n### Development\n\n1. Start the AI server (requires `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` environment variable):\n```bash\nexport ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_api_key_here\nbun run start:server\n```\n\nThe server will start on port 8080.\n\n2. In another terminal, run the example app:\n```bash\nbun run dev\n```\n\nThis will start a dev server at http://localhost:3000\n\n### Build\n\nBuild all packages:\n```bash\nbun run build\n```\n\nBuild individual packages:\n```bash\nbun run build:client\nbun run build:server\n```\n\n## Packages\n\n### @use-ai/client\n\nReact hooks library for AI integrations using WebMCP (Model Context Protocol). Features:\n- `UseAIProvider` context component for WebSocket connection configuration\n- `useAI` hook that accepts tool definitions for AI agent function calling\n- Automatic tool execution and result streaming\n\n### @use-ai/server\n\nWebSocket server that hosts AI agents and proxies requests to Claude API. Features:\n- WebSocket-based client communication\n- MCP tool registration and execution\n- Conversation history management\n- Claude API integration\n\n### example\n\nAn AI-powered todo list application demonstrating the use-ai library. The AI can:\n- Add, delete, and toggle todos via natural language\n- Query the current todo list\n- Understand context and perform multiple operations\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- **Runtime**: Bun\n- **Language**: TypeScript\n- **UI Framework**: React\n- **AI Model**: Claude (Anthropic)\n- **Protocol**: WebSocket + WebMCP\n- **Build Tool**: Bun bundler\n\n## Usage Example\n\n```tsx\nimport { UseAIProvider, useAI } from '@use-ai/client';\n\nfunction App() {\n  const { response, loading, generate } = useAI({\n    tools: {\n      addTodo: {\n        fn: (input) => addTodo(input.text),\n        config: {\n          description: 'Add a new todo item',\n          parameters: {\n            text: { type: 'string', required: true }\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button onClick={() => generate('Add a todo for grocery shopping')}>\n        Ask AI\n      </button>\n      {response && <p>{response}</p>}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\n// Wrap with provider\n<UseAIProvider serverUrl=\"ws://localhost:8080\">\n  <App />\n</UseAIProvider>\n```",
